
PCA:
To evaluate the intrinsic similarities and dis-
criminations among samples, spectral principal component analysis
(PCA) was conducted using Matlab (version R2013a). SIMS data were
treated by the following steps: normalization to the total ion intensity of
selected peaks, square root transformation, and mean-centering, prior
to spectral PCA (Sui et al., 2017) after removing known interference
peaks in the rst round of analysis followed with selected peak spectral
PCA. In the second round of spectral PCA, peaks were chosen based on
the following criteria: (a) the loading of a peak was signi cantly higher
than its neighboring peaks, (b) the intensity of the peak in the SIMS
mass spectrum was 3 times higher than the its neighboring peaks, (c)
the peak intensity was more than 0.5% of the total ion intensities, and
(d) product peaks identi ed in previous papers were included in this
study (Ding et al., 2016; Sui et al., 2017).


