 In order to extract more data information, PCA technique is
employed in this study. PCA provides an outline information of
the contamination from the surrounding surface. The factor
loadings presented in the image scores from the PC differs across
a similar analysis area. Theoretically, the factor loading of PC1
has the strongest influence over the entire mass range due to a
phenomenon known as topographical effects [6] which
potentially affects all or most of the mass peak intensities
uniformly. As all mass fragments are affected under this influence,
PC1 accounts for the majority of mass variance.
